Aim
To simulate a quality control system using GPSS and study the inspection process using multiple machines.

Theory
A Quality Control System is used in industries to inspect products and ensure that they meet required quality standards before delivery to customers.
In this simulation, products arrive for inspection and enter a waiting queue. Multiple machines or workers perform quality checks on the products. If all machines are busy, products wait in the queue.
The GENERATE block creates products. The QUEUE block stores products in the waiting line. The SEIZE block assigns inspection machines to the products. 
The DEPART block removes the products from the queue when inspection starts.
The ADVANCE block represents inspection time. The RELEASE block frees the machine after inspection.

The simulation helps in analyzing:

Machine utilization
Queue length
Product waiting time
Inspection efficiency

Applications:

Manufacturing industries
Automobile industries
Electronics industries
Pharmaceutical industries

Advantages:

Improves product quality
Reduces defective products
Increases customer satisfaction
Enhances production efficiency

Conclusion

Thus, the simulation of a quality control system was successfully implemented using GPSS. 
The experiment demonstrated the use of multiple machines for inspection and showed how queues and service times affect system performance.
